  "verbalization": "Cassialactone is shown to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the cell line SMMC-7721. The first pathway links Cassialactone to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, a compound that in turn targets SMMC-7721. A second pathway connects Cassialactone to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is also targeted by the same chromone compound, reinforcing the role of this pathway in mediating the effect on SMMC-7721. A third pathway reveals that Cassialactone targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is targeted by a more complex molecule that also targets SMMC-7721. These findings suggest that Cassialactone exerts its effects through multiple distinct molecular mechanisms, all of which ultimately contribute to the observed interaction with SMMC-7721. The evidence supports a complex, multi-targeted interaction, with the strength of the relationship varying across the different pathways.",
